{"id":199710012226943,"type":"album","name":"The Crane Wife","artist":"The Decemberists","year":2006,"weight":10,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/the-crane-wife-1.jpg","aoty":79,"aoty_user":83,"yt":"HrEoiiF0obM","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-decemberists/the-crane-wife","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/441-the-decemberists-the-crane-wife.php"},"desc":"The Crane Wife is an album by The Decemberists, released in 2006. It was produced by Tucker Martine and Chris Walla, and is the band's first album on the Capitol Records label. The album was inspired by a Japanese folk tale, and centers on two song cycles, The Crane Wife and The Island, the latter of which was inspired by William Shakespeare's The Tempest. National Public Radio listeners voted The Crane Wife the best album of 2006. The album cover was made by Portland artist Carson Ellis, long-time girlfriend (and now wife) of Colin Meloy, who has created artwork for ."},"artist_ref":{"id":243690770200536,"name":"The Decemberists","info":{"img":null}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":194427380844280,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":621,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":135494496540693,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":340,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":14904231609010,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Folk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":264,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":216253704998822,"name":"RYM Top — Folk — Indie Folk","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":40,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":44844465110460,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Folk Rock","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":77,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":82075953765266,"name":"RYM Top — Pop — Indie Pop","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":80,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruff